{"number": 74, "text": "      34             The       economy\n\n\n                     Budget    speech\n\n                                                        As we can all testify, this country’s economy is strong and\n                                                        getting stronger.\n                                                        Our  measures to curb inflation’ have proved highly\n                                                        successful. The rampant  inflation’ of the previous\n                                                         government  is a thing of the past. Inflation currently stands\n                                                         at 2 percent. The strength of the current economic climate\n                                                         suggests that interest rates are unlikely to be raised\n                                                         again this year. This should help us to build up a culture of\n                                                         investing for the long-term.\n                                                         This government has steered the economy   through seven\n                                                         years of uninterrupted economic growth;  a trend which\n                                                         is set to continue with our major success in stimulating\n                                                         growth. And in the latest quarter, the economy has been\n                     |     A                             growing at an annual rate of 2.5 percent.  :\n                                                         All indicators show that industry is thriving’. But we are\n                                                         particularly proud of the steady growth experienced by\n                                                         small businesses. We have made it our aim to safeguard\n                                                         their interests’ and the healthy economy we have created\n                                                         has enabled them to increase output. The plummeting\n                                                         profits’ caused by the previous government’s misguided\n                                                         policies are now safely behind them.\n                                                         Our goal is to establish world-class public services through\n                                                         investment and reform in order to ensure that taxpayers\n                                                         receive real value for money. Public spending goes to\n                                                         provide strong and dependable public services. These are\n                                                         vital to extend opportunity, tackle social exclusion® and\n                                                         improve people’s life chances.\n                        The taxes that we levy’ allow us to allocate resources to achieve that goal. And we have met\n                        with considerable success’. In particular, we must now build on the success’ of the climate-\n                        change  levy we introduced  last year.\n                        Another  of our goals is to win the battle against the black economy. If left        the\n                         black economy - | think here particularly of the loss to our economy of undeclared earnings”\n                         and other tax-evasion practices - will push up     and lead to rising unemployment.  This\n                         government  is committed to its eradication.\n\n\n                      1 control inflation [continuous increase in prices] 7 impose or introduce\n                                                                       been very successful\n                     ? very dramatic, uncontrolled inflation\n                                                                      ° develop previous success\n                      3 doing very well\n                                                                     10 not stopped\n                       protect their interests\n                                                                     11 income that people fail to report to the tax\n                      5 rapidly falling profits\n                       the problems of the underprivileged, of those who authorities\n                       have less fortunate places in society than others 12 make costs rise\n\n\n       72             English Collocations in Use Advanced", "char_count": 4655, "mean_conf": 92.55, "word_count": 406, "words": [{"text": "Budget", "x0": 426, "y0": 420, "x1": 602, "y1": 473, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "speech", "x0": 616, "y0": 419, "x1": 790, "y1": 470, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "As", "x0": 1135, "y0": 544, "x1": 1178, "y1": 575, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "we", "x0": 1191, "y0": 551, "x1": 1244, "y1": 574, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "can", "x0": 1257, "y0": 551, "x1": 1321, "y1": 574, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "all", "x0": 1336, "y0": 540, "x1": 1379, "y1": 573, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "testify,", "x0": 1391, "y0": 539, "x1": 1516, "y1": 582, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "this", "x0": 1529, "y0": 540, "x1": 1598, "y1": 572, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "country’s", "x0": 1611, "y0": 539, "x1": 1786, "y1": 580, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "economy", "x0": 1798, "y0": 547, "x1": 1972, "y1": 580, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "is", "x0": 1986, "y0": 538, "x1": 2012, "y1": 570, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "strong", "x0": 2026, "y0": 541, "x1": 2145, "y1": 579, "conf": 95, "bold": false}, {"text": "and", "x0": 2158, "y0": 536, "x1": 2225, "y1": 570, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text"